#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. A channel name was given for a shun or Z-line.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): G-line.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.channelGlineOnly"
msgid "Only a G-line can ban a channel name."
msgstr "Забанить имя канала может только G-line."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. The /bits after the address are more than the address has.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): CIDR.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.cidrTooLong"
msgid "That CIDR has more bits than an address."
msgstr "В этом CIDR больше битов, чем в адресе."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. The field is empty.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.empty"
msgid "Enter a mask."
msgstr "Введите маску."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. Nothing after the '@'.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.emptyHost"
msgid "The host part is empty."
msgstr "Часть хоста пуста."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. An unknown $-mask was given.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): $R, $V, CTCP; translate 'realname' and 'version'.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.extended"
msgid "Only $R (realname) and $V (CTCP version) masks exist."
msgstr "Существуют только маски $R (реальное имя) и $V (версия CTCP)."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. '*.com' is an example mask: keep it exactly. A label is a dot-separated part of a host name.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.lastLabels"
msgid "No wildcards in the last two labels (*.com bans the world)."
msgstr "Без шаблонов в двух последних частях (*.com банит весь мир)."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. '?' is the one-character wildcard: keep it exactly.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.spaces"
msgid "A mask cannot contain spaces (use ? for one)."
msgstr "Маска не может содержать пробелы (используйте ? вместо пробела)."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. The address range is too wide.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): /16.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.tooWide"
msgid "Wider than /16: the server refuses it even forced."
msgstr "Шире /16: сервер отклоняет даже принудительно."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. A host mask with * or ? must have at least three labels (a.b.c).
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.twoDots"
msgid "A wildcard host needs at least two dots."
msgstr "Хосту с шаблоном нужны минимум две точки."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask. A $R/$V mask was given for a Z-line.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): Z-line, IP.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.zlineIpOnly"
msgid "Z-lines take IP masks only."
msgstr "Z-line принимает только IP-маски."

#. Error under the mask field of the oper's ban dialog: the server would refuse this ban mask.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): Z-line, IP, CIDR.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.zlineMask"
msgid "Z-line masks must be an IP address or CIDR."
msgstr "Маска Z-line должна быть IP-адресом или CIDR."

#. A mask suggestion in the oper's ban dialog (G-line, shun or Z-line), shown beside the mask it stands for. ≤ 30 characters. Bans the user's host name.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.suggest.host"
msgid "This host name"
msgstr "Это имя хоста"

#. A mask suggestion in the oper's ban dialog (G-line, shun or Z-line), shown beside the mask it stands for. ≤ 30 characters. Bans only this ident (username) from the user's IP.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): ident, IP.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.suggest.identIp"
msgid "This ident on this IP"
msgstr "Этот ident с этого IP"

#. A mask suggestion in the oper's ban dialog (G-line, shun or Z-line), shown beside the mask it stands for. ≤ 30 characters. Bans the user's IP address.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): IP.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.suggest.ip"
msgid "This IP"
msgstr "Этот IP"

#. A mask suggestion in the oper's ban dialog (G-line, shun or Z-line), shown beside the mask it stands for. ≤ 30 characters. Bans the user's whole /24 IPv4 network (256 addresses).
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): /24.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.suggest.slash24"
msgid "The /24"
msgstr "Вся /24"

#. A mask suggestion in the oper's ban dialog (G-line, shun or Z-line), shown beside the mask it stands for. ≤ 30 characters. Bans the whole /24 network; the server accepts such a wide ban only when forced.
#. Keep as is (IRC jargon): /24, force.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.suggest.slash24Force"
msgid "The /24 (needs force)"
msgstr "Вся /24 (нужен force)"

#. A ban type, put into a server-notice sentence as its {type} (beside G-line, Z-line and shun, which stay as is): a ban on a channel name. Lower case, ≤ 20 characters, a noun phrase that reads inside '… added a global {type} on #chan'.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/noticeText.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.type.channel"
msgid "channel ban"
msgstr "бан канала"

